{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '300,370p;500,780p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   301\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   302\t   cursor cell.\"\n   303\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   304\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   305\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   306\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   307\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   308\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   309\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   313\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route the\n   314\t   retained call had on the emitter: the cursor entry under\n   315\t   `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, reading the call-out stream under\n   316\t   `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its kept position. nil when the\n   317\t   composition holds no call pair, which no real retained request\n   318\t   does -- the pair is checked before the call parked.\"\n   319\t  [resources]\n   320\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   321\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   322\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   323\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   324\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   325\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   329\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   330\t   the request the engine holds unsent. Both endpoints are served --\n   331\t   the request stream's marker and the response stream's marker,\n   332\t   `call-out-cell`'s -- and the retained envelope rides VERBATIM\n   333\t   (`:yin.k/request-envelope`) beside the kept response cell\n   334\t   (`:yin.k/response-cell`), its op and args carried only as\n   335\t   derived views (`:request-op`, `:request-args`; the op is the\n   336\t   source of the lowered entry's `:op`), so a resumer re-establishes\n   337\t   the carried pair exactly as the sender held it: retry through the\n   338\t   request reflection, wait for the response through the response\n   339\t   reflection at the kept position. The envelope is the whole truth:\n   340\t   the request protocol is open to keys beyond op and args\n   341\t   (`dao.stream.apply`'s `request?`), so the lower must never\n   342\t   rebuild it from the views. Either endpoint unservable refuses as\n   343\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that endpoint's identity, before any\n   344\t   value is minted.\"\n   345\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   346\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   347\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   348\t        route (call-out-cell resources)\n   349\t        resp-h (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))]\n   350\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   351\t      (if-let [resp-marker (and resp-h (lift-marker serve! resp-h))]\n   352\t        (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id route) resp-h (:cursor route))]\n   353\t          {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   354\t                     :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   355\t                     :yin.k/request-envelope envelope,\n   356\t                     :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   357\t                                           (:op entry)),\n   358\t                     :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   359\t                     :yin.k/request marker,\n   360\t                     :yin.k/response resp-marker,\n   361\t                     :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   362\t           :cell? true}\n   363\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   364\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   365\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t(defn- lift-link\n   369\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   370\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   500\t        (recur (inc n))\n   501\t        (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n   502\t\n   503\t\n   504\t(defn- pending-markers\n   505\t  \"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\n   506\t   target of a put, both endpoints of a retained call, the pair of\n   507\t   a link request.\"\n   508\t  [pending]\n   509\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   510\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\n   511\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   512\t                  (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   513\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   514\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   515\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   516\t    []))\n   517\t\n   518\t\n   519\t(defn- attach-all\n   520\t  \"One attach per distinct stream identity. The first attach that\n   521\t   does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone included -- refuses\n   522\t   the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that identity. Returns\n   523\t   {:handles {identity handle}}; `lower-frame` allocates each\n   524\t   reflection its own collision-free resource key.\"\n   525\t  [attach! markers]\n   526\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\n   527\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\n   528\t                      {} markers)]\n   529\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\n   530\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\n   531\t                   (assoc-in acc [:handles identity] h)\n   532\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\n   533\t               {:handles {}}\n   534\t               by-id)))\n   535\t\n   536\t\n   537\t(defn- cell-resources\n   538\t  \"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to, under the key\n   539\t   `cell-keys` allocated for it: its carried position, on the\n   540\t   reflection of the stream the cell names. Two references to one\n   541\t   cell share the one entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own\n   542\t   (S7.5.3); equal cell ids across separately lowered frames got\n   543\t   different keys, so no two frames ever share an entry. A response\n   544\t   route is no exception: it lowers under its own fresh key, never\n   545\t   at a fixed key, so distinct routes stay distinct and no migrated\n   546\t   route can ever misroute a new call.\"\n   547\t  [streams cells cell-keys]\n   548\t  (into {}\n   549\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\n   550\t               [(cell-keys cid)\n   551\t                {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\n   552\t                 :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\n   553\t        cells))\n   554\t\n   555\t\n   556\t(defn- link-pair-resources\n   557\t  \"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\n   558\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\n   559\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\n   560\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\n   561\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\n   562\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\n   563\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\n   564\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\"\n   565\t  [streams resources pendings]\n   566\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   567\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n   568\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   569\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   570\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   571\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   572\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\n   573\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   574\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\n   575\t                (if (and req resp)\n   576\t                  (assoc acc\n   577\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\n   578\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\n   579\t                  acc))\n   580\t              acc))\n   581\t          {}\n   582\t          pendings))\n   583\t\n   584\t\n   585\t(defn- lower-one\n   586\t  \"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\n   587\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\n   588\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\n   589\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\n   590\t   stream identity where one is known. Every wait polls the key\n   591\t   `cell-keys` allocated for its cell, reading the stream key\n   592\t   `streams` allocated for the cell's reflection: migrated waits\n   593\t   poll routes no new call shares. A retained request's retry\n   594\t   writes through the request reflection's allocated key and stamps\n   595\t   the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\n   596\t   `:response-stream`) for its restore; its `:datom` is the carried\n   597\t   envelope itself, never a rebuild from the op/args views (the\n   598\t   request protocol is open to further keys) -- a `:ffi-request`\n   599\t   pend without `:yin.k/request-envelope` is malformed and refuses\n   600\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the request identity.\"\n   601\t  [pending ctx streams cells cell-keys]\n   602\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   603\t    :next\n   604\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   605\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   606\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   607\t                       {:reason :next,\n   608\t                        :stream-id sid,\n   609\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   610\t                                     :id (cell-keys cid)}})}\n   611\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   612\t\n   613\t    :put\n   614\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\n   615\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   616\t      {:entry (merge ctx\n   617\t                     {:reason :put,\n   618\t                      :stream-id sid,\n   619\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\n   620\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\n   621\t\n   622\t    :ffi\n   623\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   624\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   625\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   626\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\n   627\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   628\t                                :stream-id sid,\n   629\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   630\t                                             :id (cell-keys cid)}}\n   631\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\n   632\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\n   633\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   634\t\n   635\t    :ffi-request\n   636\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   637\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   638\t          resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   639\t                                   :dao.stream/identity])\n   640\t          envelope (:yin.k/request-envelope pending)]\n   641\t      (if (some? envelope)\n   642\t        (if-let [req (streams req-id)]\n   643\t          (if-let [resp (streams resp-id)]\n   644\t            {:entry (merge ctx\n   645\t                           {:reason :put,\n   646\t                            :request-sent true,\n   647\t                            :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   648\t                            :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\n   649\t                            :stream-id req,\n   650\t                            :datom envelope,\n   651\t                            :response-cursor\n   652\t                            (cell-keys (:yin.k/response-cell pending)),\n   653\t                            :response-stream resp})}\n   654\t            (unsatisfied resp-id))\n   655\t          (unsatisfied req-id))\n   656\t        (unsatisfied req-id)))\n   657\t\n   658\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   659\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   660\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\n   661\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\n   662\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   663\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   664\t      (if (and sid req)\n   665\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   666\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\n   667\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\n   668\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\n   669\t                                :request module/link-request-resource,\n   670\t                                :response module/link-response-resource,\n   671\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\n   672\t                         (= :link-request reason)\n   673\t                         (assoc :envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending))))}\n   674\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   675\t\n   676\t    :install\n   677\t    {:entry (merge ctx\n   678\t                   {:reason :install, :name (:yin.k/name pending)})}\n   679\t\n   680\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\n   681\t     :yin.k/reason (:yin.k/reason pending)}))\n   682\t\n   683\t\n   684\t(defn- occupied-keys\n   685\t  \"The resource keys `receiver-resources` already holds: its own keys\n   686\t   when it is the receiver's resource table, itself when it is a\n   687\t   plain collection of keys.\"\n   688\t  [receiver-resources]\n   689\t  (if (map? receiver-resources)\n   690\t    (keys receiver-resources)\n   691\t    receiver-resources))\n   692\t\n   693\t\n   694\t(defn lower-frame\n   695\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together as one\n   696\t   batch: `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one private\n   697\t   resource key allocated per distinct served identity and one per\n   698\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\n   699\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3);\n   700\t   equal cell ids across separately lowered frames get different\n   701\t   keys. `receiver-resources` is the receiver's existing resource\n   702\t   table (or any collection of the resource keys it already holds):\n   703\t   every allocated key is checked against it, against the VM's fixed\n   704\t   resource keys, and against keys already allocated in the batch,\n   705\t   regenerating on collision -- a cross-frame collision is\n   706\t   structurally impossible, the lower cannot run without it. With\n   707\t   the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\n   708\t   `lift-frame` gives. Where the engine resolves a wait at one of its\n   709\t   own fixed resource keys, the lower parks the wait there: a link\n   710\t   wait's pair under `module/link-request-resource` and\n   711\t   `module/link-response-resource`. A retained request's retry\n   712\t   writes through its carried request reflection's allocated key and\n   713\t   stamps the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\n   714\t   `:response-stream`) for its restore. A `:ffi-request` pend\n   715\t   without its verbatim envelope is malformed: the whole frame\n   716\t   refuses before ANY attachment -- a refusal must mint no\n   717\t   reflection. `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each entry's\n   718\t   register context, merged verbatim.\"\n   719\t  [attach! pendings cells contexts receiver-resources]\n   720\t  (if-let [refusal (some (fn [pending]\n   721\t                           (when (and (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   722\t                                      (nil? (:yin.k/request-envelope pending)))\n   723\t                             (unsatisfied\n   724\t                               (get-in pending\n   725\t                                       [:yin.k/request :dao.stream/identity]))))\n   726\t                         pendings)]\n   727\t    refusal\n   728\t    (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\n   729\t                               (concat (map :yin.k/stream (vals cells))\n   730\t                                       (mapcat pending-markers pendings))))\n   731\t          a (attach-all attach! ms)]\n   732\t      (if (contains? a :yin.k/status)\n   733\t        a\n   734\t        (let [used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys\n   735\t                               (occupied-keys receiver-resources)))\n   736\t              handles (:handles a)\n   737\t              streams (into {}\n   738\t                            (map (fn [identity]\n   739\t                                   [identity (fresh-key used)]))\n   740\t                            (sort-by str (keys handles)))\n   741\t              resources (into {}\n   742\t                              (map (fn [[identity sid]]\n   743\t                                     [sid (handles identity)]))\n   744\t                              streams)\n   745\t              cell-keys (into {}\n   746\t                              (map (fn [cid] [cid (fresh-key used)]))\n   747\t                              (sort-by str (keys cells)))\n   748\t              lowered (mapv #(lower-one %1 %2 streams cells cell-keys)\n   749\t                            pendings contexts)]\n   750\t          (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %)\n   751\t                                 lowered)]\n   752\t            refusal\n   753\t            {:entries (mapv :entry lowered),\n   754\t             :resources (merge resources\n   755\t                               (cell-resources streams cells cell-keys)\n   756\t                               (link-pair-resources streams resources\n   757\t                                                    pendings))}))))))\n   758\t\n   759\t\n   760\t(defn lower-pending\n   761\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e, :resources\n   762\t   table}` -- the wait-set entry `ctx`'s registers ride on, and the\n   763\t   fresh resource entries it polls through -- with the same\n   764\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\n   765\t   `lower-frame` gives. `receiver-resources` is the receiver's\n   766\t   existing resource table (or key collection), as `lower-frame`'s:\n   767\t   batch allocation regenerates against what is already installed.\n   768\t   Frame assembly that shares cursor entries across entries is\n   769\t   `lower-frame`'s.\"\n   770\t  [attach! pending cells ctx receiver-resources]\n   771\t  (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx] receiver-resources)]\n   772\t    (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   773\t      r\n   774\t      (-> r\n   775\t          (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\n   776\t          (dissoc :entries)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
